  "result": "The concept and its witnesses are written, but the gate hasn't judged them. Both runs I made (2 of 6) stopped at **SCOPE_VIOLATION** before checking any Lean.\n\n**Why the gate failed:** it flagged files under `.runtime/tmp/.../tasks/*.output`, which is where the agent tooling saves each shell command's output. I didn't write them, and since the shell may run only the gate command, I can't remove them. The second run also flagged one from another session running at the same time (`…drv-motion-compl…`), so the check is reading a temp folder that all sessions share. The harness's scope check needs to ignore `.runtime/`. Until then, more runs of mine would get the same verdict, so I stopped there.\n\n**Concept body** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/moving_against_carrier.lean`): a's velocity along r's direction, `vx·dx + vy·dy`, must be below `−speed_tol`.\n- Core already scales `st_lane_direction` to a unit vector when a formula reads it, which is the normalising the contract asks for.\n- If a's velocity or r's direction is missing, the result is unknown.\n- It uses only the two atoms the record claims and its one parameter. The contract left no choices open, so there are no narrowings.\n\n**Witnesses:** lane 100 is the rectangle x 0–100 m, y −2 to 2 m, with direction east. Road user 1 is a motor vehicle standing at (50, 0). The instance sets `speed_tol` to 0.1 m/s.\n- **holds:** velocity (−5, 0) m/s, so the component is −5 and the expected result is compliant.\n- **fails:** velocity (5, 0.2) m/s, so the component is +5 and the expected result is violated.\n- **blind:** velocity is unset and `kin.velocity` is masked, so the expected result is unknown.\n\nI found nothing wrong with the record. `task_result.md` in the working directory has the run log and these details.",
